    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450">

                <pb facs="0520" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00 Revolutions/376: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-09-21T19:00:00-03:00">September 21,
                            1932—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>110. On learning on September 19 that Campinas had been bombarded by Federal
                    forces I verbally protested to Foreign Minister. On learning today of injury to
                    property of Bond and Share I again protested verbally. Minister recognizes
                    propriety of representation but states that aviation corps is uncontrolled and
                    irresponsible.</p>
                <p>Have requested urgent audience with Dr. Getulio
                        Vargas to represent that the situation caused by bombardment of
                    an open town is already grave and will become’ more so if through bombardment
                    American lives are lost.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
